│ index (BMIsd) compared to baseline. Nereu Program participants (n = 54) showed greater increases in moderate-intense │
│ physical activity (+6.27% vs. -0.61%, p<0.001) and daily fruit servings (+0.62 vs. +0.13, p<0.026), and decreased    │
│ daily soft drinks consumption (-0.26 vs. -0.02, p<0.047), respectively, compared to the counselling group (n = 59).  │
│ CONCLUSIONS At the end of the 8-month intervention, participants in the Nereu Program group showed improvement in    │
│ physical activity and dietary behaviours, compared to the counselling group. TRIAL REGISTRATION ClinicalTrials.gov   │
│ NCT01878994."}, {"study_index": 93, "title": "Reducing children\'s television viewing to prevent obesity: a          │
│ randomized controlled trial", "abstract": "CONTEXT Some observational studies have found an association between      │
