  observed in parental BMI scores from pre- to post- treatment (F(1.59)= 71.54, p%lt;0.001) but a significant increase  
  was evident at one year post-treatment (F(1.59)=41.87, p%lt;0.001). Improvements were observed for measures of        
  parental depression from pre- to post- treatment (F(1.60)= 12.93, p<0.01). CONCLUSION Epstein´s family-based          
  behavioural treatment showed promising effects on weight status, and emotional as well as physical markers, both in   
